WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.862
Long and wide are not quality levels.

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:05.562
They are different ways to arrange information.

00:00:05.562 --> 00:00:09.527
Long data usually stores categories as row values.

00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:13.627
Wide data turns selected category values into columns.

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:17.187
The dangerous part is that many pivots also aggregate.

00:00:17.187 --> 00:00:23.062
When several source rows map to one pivot cell, detail may be permanently removed.

00:00:23.062 --> 00:00:29.077
Connect this idea to a machine-learning workflow converting wide measurements into tidy long data.

00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:34.552
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.552 --> 00:00:41.502
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.502 --> 00:00:46.857
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.857 --> 00:00:52.160
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
